	(text "Cut-off at 1.6 V, 3.3 V boost, LED rail switch"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290.952 45 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3 3)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "eac20d0f-7a36-54cf-9322-ba102ee8a54f")
	)
	(text "TPS61299: 95 nA quiescent, 1.2 A input limit: about 470 mA at 3.3 V from a 1.9 V cell. Firmware caps the LED current."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290.952 52 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c1424aa1-42b1-5e12-bfb2-d441e8c4ac92")
	)
	(text "VSEL straight to GND = 3.3 V. Nothing higher: 3.5 V +2 % and the light-load offset is over the ESP32's 3.6 V maximum."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290.952 55 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dd53d70e-2f9b-5306-9b19-ea634cb13395")
	)
	(text "TPS3840PL16 holds the boost off below 1.6 V and lets it back on at 1.7 V. The cell rests at 1.98 V when empty and is rated to 1.5 V:"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290.952 58 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "799aee86-295a-5641-a185-8d473f849a7d")
	)
	(text "a 2.0 V part sits inside the flat bottom of its curve and trips on load sag from 10 to 30 % charge (layout review)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290.952 61 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0ff8b579-4e8e-519f-91d6-e69ce5c78fe1")
	)
	(text "Its supply is filtered (10k, 1u) so a transmit burst's sag does not trip it. PL18 (1.8 V, C1852123) fits the same pads: none in stock."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290.952 64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "740ed0e6-25cd-5812-b269-aea469fe82de")
	)
	(text "Firmware reads VBAT before the radio starts and sleeps below 2.05 V: the cut-off is under the empty cell's rest voltage, so this is what keeps it from boot-looping."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290.952 67 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c87f51d6-4228-5b1d-ac14-86a0c6ee5542")
	)
	(text "VBAT_SENSE goes straight to the ADC (0..2.5 V range): 470k in series (pin leakage of 50 nA is then 24 mV, not 50), and a dead 3V3 rail draws about 3 uA through the pin."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290.952 70 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e2d0ce3c-2171-50a1-84a8-8166ab4dacf5")
	)
	(text "First power-up: no cell, BOOST_EN's pad held to GND, USB in, VBAT must read 2.40 V. An open joint on the 200k feedback resistor sends VBAT to 5 V,"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290.952 73 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ad5abbbd-0012-52d7-bfea-23a4eef11cb6")
	)
	(text "and the boost passes anything over 3.4 V straight to the module."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290.952 76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "197ee6f8-65ef-57a7-b734-1766e9becf1f")
	)
	(text "LED rail: TPS22919, 1.1 ms rise, discharges VLED when off. LED_EN floats at reset: the 100k keeps it off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290.952 79 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6b8c4d14-9f9b-51a4-9627-a7de99e3fa36")
	)
